How FFmpeg is used
- native/build.sh builds FFmpeg 8.1.3 as static libraries (libavformat,
  libavcodec, libavutil) and links them with native/remux.c into one shared
  library, libmovmp4.so, per Android ABI. The configuration is LGPL only: no
  --enable-gpl, no --enable-nonfree, no codecs; only the MOV demuxer, the MP4
  muxer, the parsers and the aac_adtstoasc, vp9_superframe and
  extract_extradata bitstream filters. The exact configure flags are in
  native/build.sh.
- native/build.sh applies no patches to the FFmpeg source.
- The prebuilt app/src/main/jniLibs/*/libmovmp4.so files and any APK built from
  this repository contain that FFmpeg code.

